      "problem": "$8\\cdot (-5)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of a positive number $(8)$ and a negative number $(-5).$ So the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n8\\cdot (-5)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $8$ by $5$ without any signs: $8\\cdot 5=40.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n8\\cdot (-5)=-40.\n$$",
